# .trivyignore - Trivy false positives exclusion
# Documentation: https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/

# ====================================================================
# IMPORTANT: FILE EXCLUSIONS FOR SECRET SCANNING
# ====================================================================
# This file (.trivyignore) is used to ignore specific VULNERABILITIES (by CVE ID).
# To ignore ENTIRE FILES from secret scanning, we use --skip-files in:
#   - .github/workflows/security-scan.yml (skip-files parameter)
#   - security-scan.sh (--skip-files flag)
#
# Files currently skipped from secret scanning:
#   - .env              (Docker/K8s placeholders, not real secrets)
#   - .env.test         (Mock test credentials)
#   - CI_CD.md          (Documentation with examples)
#   - README.md         (Documentation with examples)
#   - QUICKSTART.md     (Documentation with examples)
#
# ====================================================================
# VULNERABILITY EXCLUSIONS (CVE-based)
# ====================================================================
# Use this file to ignore specific vulnerabilities by CVE ID or package name.
# Format:
#   CVE-2023-12345
#   pkg:composer/vendor/package@1.2.3
#
# Example to ignore a specific CVE:
# CVE-2023-46733
#
# Example to ignore all vulnerabilities in a specific package:
# php-http/message@1.0.0
#
# ====================================================================
# FALSE POSITIVES - Add below
# ====================================================================

# Add CVE IDs or package identifiers here if needed
